  "rootCause": "Conformal coating applied at 18°C, below the 22°C specification minimum, due to HVAC system being under repair, combined with QC accepting units based solely on visual inspection without functional testing at temperature extremes.",
  "actions": "Repair HVAC system to maintain minimum 22°C ambient temperature; implement process interlocks to halt production if temperature falls below specification; update QC protocol to require functional testing at temperature extremes (-40°C to -20°C) for all electronic control modules; retrain production and QC staff on new procedures.",
  "evidence": "HVAC maintenance records confirming repair and temperature logs showing compliance with 22°C minimum; updated QC protocol documentation including functional test requirements at temperature extremes; training records for production and QC staff; functional test results for subsequent production lots demonstrating no failures at -40°C to -20°C."
